\begin{abstract}
%Should not normally exceed 200 words.
Two-particle high-\pT triggered correlations involving strange particles in \Cu and \Au collisions at \sNNtwohundred in STAR at RHIC are presented.  The \npart, \ptassoc, and \pttrig dependence of the yield per trigger in the \jet and \ridge components of the \nearside is investigated for \kaon, \lam, and \xibary trigger and \kaon and \lam associated particles.  The baryon/meson ratio in the \jet is investigated.  No dependence on the collision system is observed and no strong dependence on strangeness content is observed, in agreement with previous studies.  These data strengthen the argument that the dominant production mechanism for the \jet is vacuum fragmentation, and constrain models which would predict a strong dependence on particle trigger type or strangeness content.

\end{abstract}
