\section{Conclusions}
Neither the \jet nor the \ridge yields show dependence on trigger particle type or strangeness content.  There is no dependence on collision system.  The particle ratios in the \jet are consistent with those observed in \pp.  These observations support the data shown in \cite{PIDPaper,EnergyPaper} that imply that the dominant mechanism for the formation of the \jet component of the \nearside of \highpT correlations is fragmentation, although there is room within the errors for small contributions from other mechanisms.  These data limit the production mechanisms feasible for the \ridge to those where there is no strong dependence on system or particle type.

